We show that exactly one position survives in~each original block~$\textcolor{purple!69!black}{\mathtt{a}}^{k_{\textcolor{purple!69!black}{\mathtt{a}}}}$. At~a~boundary between original blocks, suppose that $j$ blocks of~letter~$\textcolor{purple!69!black}{\mathtt{a}}$ have been processed. If the~two copies have used $u$ and~$v$ occurrences of~$\textcolor{purple!69!black}{\mathtt{a}}$, then $u+v=k_{\textcolor{purple!69!black}{\mathtt{a}}} j$. The~number of~retained occurrences in~a~prefix containing $t$ occurrences is
\begin{align*}
